Register libvkd3d_d3d12 as a FEX thunked library.

NOT APPLIED. The FEX checkout is read-only to this work; this is the in-tree
equivalent of pe-shim/build.sh, provided so the owner can apply it
deliberately. build.sh remains the out-of-tree equivalent and needs none of
this.

Before applying, symlink the sources in (add_guest_lib/add_host_lib look for
ThunkLibs/lib<NAME>/lib<NAME>_{Guest,Host}.cpp, and this directory is named to
provide exactly that):

    cd <fex>/ThunkLibs
    ln -s <...>/vkd3d-proton/ppc64le/pe-shim libvkd3d_d3d12

Then:

    cd <fex> && git apply .../fex-registration.patch
    ninja -C build-thunks guest-libs host-libs

Two things the CMake wiring does NOT do, because they are not CMake's job:

  * install the guest .so where the PE shim's compiled-in default looks for it
    (/usr/local/lib/fex-emu/libvkd3d_d3d12-guest.so, or anywhere and set
    VKD3D_THUNK_GUEST_SO);
  * create $FEX_THUNKHOSTLIBS/libvkd3d_d3d12.so.0 as a symlink to the native
    libvkd3d-proton-d3d12.so. thunkgen's generated loader dlopens that name and
    hands FEX a null export table if it fails -- see
    libvkd3d_d3d12_interface.cpp.

The three hunks are modelled on dxvk-ppc64le/pe-shim/fastppcx86-registration.patch
and follow the libxshmfence pattern exactly, 64-bit guest only. Diffed against
the fex-ppc64le tree as of 2026-08-13; expect to fuzz-adjust the line numbers
on a different checkout.

